{
  "summary": "The refined three-part fix with conditional zero-sections guard and cache-on-all-paths is sound, but two operational gaps remain. First, there is no protection against fetch race conditions: if smartPollBoard fires overlapping requests (e.g., a slow response from poll N arrives after poll N+1 has already updated the DOM), the stale response will overwrite newer content — a sequence counter or AbortController per poll cycle is needed to discard out-of-order responses. Second, the Promise.reject() error-handling path is silent — persistent server failures (502s, timeouts) will be invisibly swallowed with no user feedback or backoff, meaning the board appears frozen with stale data and the user has no indication anything is wrong; at minimum, consecutive non-200 responses should trigger a visible status indicator or exponential backoff on the poll interval."
}
